fix: scope the Object-diet size asserts to x86_64.

heap.zig's comptime block asserts sizeOf(Thunk)==40 / sizeOf(Object)==48 in
ReleaseFast as a guard against fields creeping back in after the Object diet.
The expected sizes hold on x86_64 (upstream's build arch) but NOT on
aarch64-linux-musl, where alignment differs -- so an aarch64 ReleaseFast build
(the badge's production fix graph; ReleaseFast is REQUIRED there because fix's
gc_debug=ReleaseSafe detector deliberately never reuses freed object slots,
leaking ~160 headers/frame under compile-once/apply-per-frame) fails to
compile on this assert alone. Scope the diet guard to the arch it was written
for; it keeps its full value on x86_64 CI while unblocking aarch64.

--- a/src/runtime/heap.zig	2026-08-30 12:00:00.000000000 -0700
+++ b/src/runtime/heap.zig	2026-08-30 12:00:00.000000000 -0700
@@ -163,10 +163,13 @@
 comptime {
     // The Object diet's whole point: Thunk 48->40 (flag word folded into the
     // Future state word, effect_group in the side table) => Object 56->48.
     // ReleaseFast only - Debug carries union safety tags, prof builds carry
-    // census fields. If this fires, a field crept back in.
-    if (@import("builtin").mode == .ReleaseFast and !@import("build_options").prof_main) {
+    // census fields. If this fires, a field crept back in. x86_64 only: the
+    // dieted sizes depend on that arch's alignment (aarch64 differs).
+    if (@import("builtin").mode == .ReleaseFast and !@import("build_options").prof_main and
+        @import("builtin").cpu.arch == .x86_64)
+    {
         std.debug.assert(@sizeOf(Thunk) == 40);
         std.debug.assert(@sizeOf(Object) == 48);
     }
 }
